1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
Your map has sides now,

2
00:00:02,624 --> 00:00:04,798
but there's nobody on them.

3
00:00:05,698 --> 00:00:07,437
Today we fix that.

4
00:00:08,337 --> 00:00:10,946
We're going to write three people,

5
00:00:11,396 --> 00:00:14,439
and give each of them a face.

6
00:00:16,239 --> 00:00:19,717
It's one new section in your fact sheet,

7
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:24,080
and you won't touch the story file at all.

8
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:29,628
First, one line of the story file, just to read.

9
00:00:30,528 --> 00:00:34,876
In Lecture 11 this line was marked for Class 2.

10
00:00:35,776 --> 00:00:40,993
It makes a person from every record of a section called characters,

11
00:00:41,443 --> 00:00:44,487
so that's the key my section needs.

12
00:00:46,287 --> 00:00:51,939
Now the section itself is two hashes, the word Characters, and that key.

13
00:00:52,839 --> 00:00:55,448
Then the person, with three hashes,

14
00:00:55,898 --> 00:00:59,376
her name, and her key in round brackets.

15
00:01:00,276 --> 00:01:02,885
Inside the fence there's one line,

16
00:01:03,335 --> 00:01:05,509
Face, and the word female.

17
00:01:06,409 --> 00:01:10,322
And below the fence there's a sentence about her,

18
00:01:10,772 --> 00:01:13,380
which is a note for me.

19
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:17,759
I save, I run lint, and it's clean.

20
00:01:18,959 --> 00:01:22,002
That word female is called a keyword,

21
00:01:22,452 --> 00:01:26,365
and there are seven of them, all for humans.

22
00:01:27,265 --> 00:01:30,309
But a keyword doesn't choose a face.

23
00:01:30,759 --> 00:01:33,802
It asks the game to roll one.

24
00:01:35,602 --> 00:01:38,211
So every time the game starts,

25
00:01:38,661 --> 00:01:42,574
she gets new eyes, new hair and new clothes.

26
00:01:43,474 --> 00:01:48,691
And about half the time she gets skin that's green or blue.

27
00:01:49,591 --> 00:01:53,504
That's fine for a voice the crew hears once.

28
00:01:54,404 --> 00:01:58,317
But it's wrong for a person with a name,

29
00:01:58,767 --> 00:02:03,115
because your crew should know her when she calls again.

30
00:02:04,315 --> 00:02:09,098
To keep a face, the line has to spell it out,

31
00:02:09,548 --> 00:02:13,026
and I'm not going to type that myself.

32
00:02:13,926 --> 00:02:16,535
I press Control, Shift and P,

33
00:02:16,985 --> 00:02:21,767
which opens a box that runs any tool the editor has.

34
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:25,711
I type story graph, and press Enter.

35
00:02:27,511 --> 00:02:30,554
Here are my records, drawn as boxes,

36
00:02:31,004 --> 00:02:33,613
with one band for each section.

37
00:02:34,513 --> 00:02:37,991
I right-click Quill's box, and I choose Edit.

38
00:02:38,891 --> 00:02:41,065
This tab is the Inspector,

39
00:02:41,515 --> 00:02:44,993
and it shows her record as a form.

40
00:02:45,893 --> 00:02:50,241
Beside her face there's a button, so I click it,

41
00:02:50,691 --> 00:02:55,039
and from the list I choose a random Terran woman.

42
00:02:56,839 --> 00:02:59,013
Now look at my file.

43
00:02:59,913 --> 00:03:01,652
The keyword is gone,

44
00:03:02,102 --> 00:03:05,580
and in its place there's one long line.

45
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:09,524
That line is her face, written down.

46
00:03:10,724 --> 00:03:12,898
A roll gets me close,

47
00:03:13,348 --> 00:03:17,696
and the builder gets me the rest of the way.

48
00:03:18,596 --> 00:03:22,509
I click her picture, and the Face Builder opens,

49
00:03:22,959 --> 00:03:26,002
starting from the face she already has.

50
00:03:26,902 --> 00:03:29,511
There's a slider for each feature:

51
00:03:29,961 --> 00:03:33,004
eyes, mouth, hair, clothes and so on.

52
00:03:33,904 --> 00:03:37,383
And a tick box beside some of them

53
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:40,007
turns that feature off altogether.

54
00:03:41,807 --> 00:03:43,980
So I move the hair,

55
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:48,778
and her line in my file changes while I drag.

56
00:03:49,678 --> 00:03:51,417
There's nothing to press.

57
00:03:52,317 --> 00:03:57,970
When she looks right, I go back to the file and I save.

58
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:01,343
The second one goes faster.

59
00:04:02,243 --> 00:04:04,852
I type Chief Ives below her,

60
00:04:05,302 --> 00:04:08,346
with the keyword male, and I save.

61
00:04:09,246 --> 00:04:13,159
The graph has already drawn a box for him.

62
00:04:14,059 --> 00:04:17,102
So it's right-click, Edit, the face button,

63
00:04:17,552 --> 00:04:19,726
and a random Terran man.

64
00:04:20,626 --> 00:04:24,539
If I don't care for him, I roll again.

65
00:04:25,739 --> 00:04:28,783
My third person flies the Breaker Cutter,

66
00:04:29,233 --> 00:04:33,146
and she doesn't have to be one of us.

67
00:04:34,046 --> 00:04:36,220
The game has six peoples,

68
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:39,278
and only the humans have keywords.

69
00:04:40,178 --> 00:04:44,091
For the other five there's no word to type,

70
00:04:44,541 --> 00:04:48,020
so the editor is the only way in.

71
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:52,863
I type her record the same way,

72
00:04:53,313 --> 00:04:58,096
and this time, from the list, I choose a random Skaraan.

73
00:04:58,996 --> 00:05:04,213
And in the builder, this box at the top is her race.

74
00:05:05,413 --> 00:05:08,891
You'll copy these lines and move them about,

75
00:05:09,341 --> 00:05:13,254
and they break easily, so here are four rules.

76
00:05:14,154 --> 00:05:18,502
A face string is one line, however long it is.

77
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:23,750
You keep all of it, down to the last semicolon.

78
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:27,693
You put no quote marks round it.

79
00:05:28,593 --> 00:05:32,941
And you change it with the builder, never by hand.

80
00:05:34,741 --> 00:05:39,089
Here's what the first rule looks like when it's broken.

81
00:05:39,989 --> 00:05:42,598
I press Enter in the middle,

82
00:05:43,048 --> 00:05:47,396
and lint gives me an error on the second half.

83
00:05:48,296 --> 00:05:53,078
That's the only one of the four that lint can see,

84
00:05:53,528 --> 00:05:57,007
so the other three are yours to watch.

85
00:05:58,207 --> 00:06:01,685
And now the one that will catch you.

86
00:06:02,585 --> 00:06:04,324
I write Face, woman,

87
00:06:04,774 --> 00:06:07,817
which looks just as good as female,

88
00:06:08,267 --> 00:06:10,007
and lint says clean.

89
00:06:11,807 --> 00:06:15,285
But woman isn't one of the seven words,

90
00:06:15,735 --> 00:06:18,343
so the game doesn't roll anything.

91
00:06:19,243 --> 00:06:22,722
It takes the word itself as her face,

92
00:06:23,172 --> 00:06:25,780
and that's no face at all.

93
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:29,724
Lint knows where a person's record belongs.

94
00:06:30,174 --> 00:06:33,217
It doesn't read what comes after Face.

95
00:06:34,117 --> 00:06:38,030
So that part you check with your own eyes.

96
00:06:39,230 --> 00:06:44,013
Nobody speaks yet, so the game has nothing new to show.

97
00:06:44,913 --> 00:06:48,826
But I can look at my cast right here.

98
00:06:49,726 --> 00:06:51,900
I click inside her record,

99
00:06:52,350 --> 00:06:56,698
I open that box again, and I type preview node.

100
00:06:57,598 --> 00:07:03,250
There's Quill, and she'll look like that in every game from now on.

101
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:06,759
And there's Ives, and there's Sable.

102
00:07:07,959 --> 00:07:12,741
Now it's your turn: add a fourth person of your own,

103
00:07:13,191 --> 00:07:15,800
from a people you haven't used.

104
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:22,352
Roll a face, and then change two things about it in the builder.

105
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:27,630
Next time, the harbormaster picks up the microphone.
